    {
      "dom_id": "question-340017",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the function $y=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3{e}^{x},$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+3{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+3{e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+3{e}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2}{x}+3{e}^{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1}+3{e}^{1} \\\\  & =2+3e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
